---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="About | KB Compressor"
  description="About KB Compressor, a free browser-based tool for compressing images to an exact KB size."
>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-16">
    <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">About KB Compressor</h1>
    <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
      <p>
        KB Compressor exists because most image compressors ask the wrong question. They
        offer a "high / medium / low" quality slider, when the thing you actually need is
        much more specific: a college application portal, a job application form, or a visa
        photo upload that rejects anything over a hard limit like 100&nbsp;KB or 240&nbsp;KB.
        Getting there by trial and error &mdash; drag the slider, re-upload, get rejected,
        try again &mdash; wastes time on forms that are often already stressful enough.
      </p>
      <p>
        This tool asks for the number you actually have (the KB limit from the form) and
        works backward from it, searching for the highest image quality that still lands at
        or under your target, rather than the other way around.
      </p>
      <p>
        Everything runs locally in your browser using the HTML Canvas API. Your photo is
        never uploaded to a server, never stored, and never leaves your device &mdash; there's
        nothing to upload to, since there's no backend at all.
      </p>
      <p>
        KB Compressor is an independent tool, not affiliated with any government agency,
        university, employer, or application portal it's used with.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
